  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (RNA-only, scVI n200, multiprofile, transformer) at 0.653. The key open question is whether multimodal fusion can improve upon this. Image-only ResNet50 is weak (0.208), so the critical test is whether fusing it with the strong RNA signal helps or hurts. config_033 takes the best-validated RNA stack (scVI n200 + multiprofile + transformer) and adds ResNet50 image features with weighted fusion, which can learn to down-weight the weaker image modality. This isolates the fusion effect while keeping all other design choices at their empirically best settings. The result will determine whether to spend remaining experiments exploring stronger image encoders (ViT-L) in multimodal mode or to confirm RNA-only as the ceiling and explore minor RNA-side variations."
}

